@prefix fhir: <http://hl7.org/fhir/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# - resource -------------------------------------------------------------------

<http://costateixeira.github.io/spenser/ExampleScenario/TaskOrderScenario> a fhir:ExampleScenario ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:id [ fhir:v "TaskOrderScenario"] ; # 
  fhir:text [
     fhir:status [ fhir:v "generated" ] ;
     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><div xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><hr/><p><b>English</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ExampleScenario TaskOrderScenario</b></p><a name=\"TaskOrderScenario\"> </a><a name=\"hcTaskOrderScenario\"> </a><p><b>url</b>: <a href=\"ExampleScenario-TaskOrderScenario.html\">Ordering through an order server</a></p><p><b>version</b>: 1.0.0</p><p><b>name</b>: TaskOrderScenario</p><p><b>title</b>: Ordering through an order server</p><p><b>status</b>: Active</p><p><b>experimental</b>: true</p><p><b>date</b>: 2026-11-13 21:21:03+0000</p><p><b>publisher</b>: José Costa Teixeira</p><p><b>contact</b>: José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"https://github.com/costateixeira\">https://github.com/costateixeira</a>, José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"mailto:you-know.it@gmail.com\">you-know.it@gmail.com</a></p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A placer puts an order and a Task on an order server. The unit polls the server, dispenses what is addressed to it, and reports back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>jurisdiction</b>: <span title=\"Codes:{http://unstats.un.org/unsd/methods/m49/m49.htm 001}\">World</span></p><p><b>purpose</b>: </p><div><p>The long way round, and the one that behaves like a real workflow.</p>\n<p>An order on a server is an authorization: it says a chocolate may be dispensed,\nnot that one should be dispensed now. Something else has to ask for it to be\nfulfilled. A Task is that something, and <code>Task.requestedPerformer</code> is the only\nplace in R5 that can name the Device meant to do the work.</p>\n<p>The unit is never connected to from outside here. It polls, which is what lets\na dispenser sit on a conference network with nothing open to it.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: placer</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Placer</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Creates the order and the Task, and closes the order once the Task is done. A Task closes itself; a MedicationRequest does not.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: server</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A plain FHIR server. It holds the order and the Task until a unit collects them, and it has to answer <code>_include=Task:focus</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: spenser</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Spenser Unit</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Acting here as a FHIR client. It takes only the work addressed to it and leaves everything else alone.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationRequest\">All FHIR Types: MedicationRequest</a> (MedicationRequest)</p><p><b>structureProfile</b>: <a href=\"StructureDefinition-SpenserRequest.html\">SpenserRequest</a></p><p><b>title</b>: The order</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>An untagged MedicationRequest, naming the unit meant to fill it in the <code>dispensingDevice</code> extension. On its own it sits there.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest: extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-active</p><p><b>title</b>: active</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created: authorized, and not yet filled.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest: extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the placer closes it. The unit does not touch the order while a Task is coordinating the work.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-Task\">All FHIR Types: Task</a> (Task)</p><p><b>title</b>: The Task</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A <code>fulfill</code> Task whose <code>focus</code> is the order and whose <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. This is what makes the order actionable.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-requested</p><p><b>title</b>: requested</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created. Every other unit polling the same server skips it.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the chocolate came out, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: dispense</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationDispense\">All FHIR Types: MedicationDispense</a> (MedicationDispense)</p><p><b>title</b>: The dispense</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>What the unit writes back, naming itself as <code>performer</code> and the order in <code>authorizingPrescription</code>.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationDispense-DispenseForTaskOrder.html\">MedicationDispense: status = completed</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>process</b></p><p><b>title</b>: Order a chocolate through an order server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Place the work, let the unit find it, and read back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>preConditions</b>: </p><div><p>The unit has been pointed at the order server and its polling is on. The unit has written its own Device on the server, so a Task can name it.</p>\n</div><p><b>postConditions</b>: </p><div><p>A chocolate has been dispensed, the dispense is on the server, the Task is completed, and the order is closed.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 1</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Nothing happens yet, and that is the point.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-active</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 2</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>code</code> is <code>fulfill</code>, <code>focus</code> is the order, <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. Leave <code>requestedPerformer</code> out and any unit polling that server may take it.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>Tag the order instead of creating a Task</td><td><div><p>Put <code>actionable</code> from common-tags in the order's <code>meta.tag</code> and skip the Task. A unit accepts both routes on every check, and <code>orderMode</code> narrows it to one. With no Task coordinating the work the unit completes the MedicationRequest itself, and step 6 does not happen.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 3</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-search-type\">FHIR Restful Interactions: search-type</a> (search-type)</p><p><b>title</b>: GET /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>GET /Task?status=requested&amp;_include=Task:focus&amp;_count=5</code>. The unit polls on a timer, and a check can also be asked for by hand. Each check looks at the first five results only, so a long queue on the server can outrun one check. The unit remembers what it has already dealt with.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Responses</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 4</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationDispense</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>The servo turns and a piece drops out, and then the unit says so. The write is queued and retried, so a server that was briefly unreachable does not cost the record.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>dispense</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>The lane is empty</td><td><div><p>The unit writes a dispense with <code>status</code> of <code>declined</code> and <code>notPerformedReason.concept</code> of <code>outofstock</code>. Whether the Task is then left open, so a refill retries it, or closed as failed, is the unit's <code>keepOrders</code> setting.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 5</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /Task/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>: <code>status</code> becomes <code>completed</code>, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>. Sent with <code>If-Match</code>, so a Task somebody else has moved on is not overwritten.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 6</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /MedicationRequest/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>. The placer closes its own order. The unit does not: it was asked to fill one Task, and it has no way of knowing whether the order authorized more than that.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></div><div xml:lang=\"pt\" lang=\"pt\"><hr/><p><b>Portuguese</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Narrativa gerada: ExampleScenario TaskOrderScenario</b></p><a name=\"pt-TaskOrderScenario\"> </a><a name=\"pt-hcTaskOrderScenario\"> </a><p><b>url</b>: <a href=\"ExampleScenario-TaskOrderScenario.html\">Ordering through an order server</a></p><p><b>version</b>: 1.0.0</p><p><b>name</b>: TaskOrderScenario</p><p><b>title</b>: Ordering through an order server</p><p><b>status</b>: Active</p><p><b>experimental</b>: true</p><p><b>date</b>: 2026-11-13 21:21:03+0000</p><p><b>publisher</b>: José Costa Teixeira</p><p><b>contact</b>: José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"https://github.com/costateixeira\">https://github.com/costateixeira</a>, José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"mailto:you-know.it@gmail.com\">you-know.it@gmail.com</a></p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A placer puts an order and a Task on an order server. The unit polls the server, dispenses what is addressed to it, and reports back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>jurisdiction</b>: <span title=\"Códigos:{http://unstats.un.org/unsd/methods/m49/m49.htm 001}\">World</span></p><p><b>purpose</b>: </p><div><p>The long way round, and the one that behaves like a real workflow.</p>\n<p>An order on a server is an authorization: it says a chocolate may be dispensed,\nnot that one should be dispensed now. Something else has to ask for it to be\nfulfilled. A Task is that something, and <code>Task.requestedPerformer</code> is the only\nplace in R5 that can name the Device meant to do the work.</p>\n<p>The unit is never connected to from outside here. It polls, which is what lets\na dispenser sit on a conference network with nothing open to it.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: placer</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Placer</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Creates the order and the Task, and closes the order once the Task is done. A Task closes itself; a MedicationRequest does not.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: server</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A plain FHIR server. It holds the order and the Task until a unit collects them, and it has to answer <code>_include=Task:focus</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: spenser</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Spenser Unit</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Acting here as a FHIR client. It takes only the work addressed to it and leaves everything else alone.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationRequest\">All FHIR Types: MedicationRequest</a> (MedicationRequest)</p><p><b>structureProfile</b>: <a href=\"StructureDefinition-SpenserRequest.html\">SpenserRequest</a></p><p><b>title</b>: The order</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>An untagged MedicationRequest, naming the unit meant to fill it in the <code>dispensingDevice</code> extension. On its own it sits there.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest: extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-active</p><p><b>title</b>: active</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created: authorized, and not yet filled.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest: extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the placer closes it. The unit does not touch the order while a Task is coordinating the work.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-Task\">All FHIR Types: Task</a> (Task)</p><p><b>title</b>: The Task</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A <code>fulfill</code> Task whose <code>focus</code> is the order and whose <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. This is what makes the order actionable.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-requested</p><p><b>title</b>: requested</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created. Every other unit polling the same server skips it.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the chocolate came out, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: dispense</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationDispense\">All FHIR Types: MedicationDispense</a> (MedicationDispense)</p><p><b>title</b>: The dispense</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>What the unit writes back, naming itself as <code>performer</code> and the order in <code>authorizingPrescription</code>.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationDispense-DispenseForTaskOrder.html\">MedicationDispense: status = completed</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>process</b></p><p><b>title</b>: Order a chocolate through an order server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Place the work, let the unit find it, and read back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>preConditions</b>: </p><div><p>The unit has been pointed at the order server and its polling is on. The unit has written its own Device on the server, so a Task can name it.</p>\n</div><p><b>postConditions</b>: </p><div><p>A chocolate has been dispensed, the dispense is on the server, the Task is completed, and the order is closed.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 1</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Nothing happens yet, and that is the point.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-active</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 2</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>code</code> is <code>fulfill</code>, <code>focus</code> is the order, <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. Leave <code>requestedPerformer</code> out and any unit polling that server may take it.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>Tag the order instead of creating a Task</td><td><div><p>Put <code>actionable</code> from common-tags in the order's <code>meta.tag</code> and skip the Task. A unit accepts both routes on every check, and <code>orderMode</code> narrows it to one. With no Task coordinating the work the unit completes the MedicationRequest itself, and step 6 does not happen.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 3</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-search-type\">FHIR Restful Interactions: search-type</a> (search-type)</p><p><b>title</b>: GET /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>GET /Task?status=requested&amp;_include=Task:focus&amp;_count=5</code>. The unit polls on a timer, and a check can also be asked for by hand. Each check looks at the first five results only, so a long queue on the server can outrun one check. The unit remembers what it has already dealt with.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Responses</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 4</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationDispense</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>The servo turns and a piece drops out, and then the unit says so. The write is queued and retried, so a server that was briefly unreachable does not cost the record.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>dispense</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>The lane is empty</td><td><div><p>The unit writes a dispense with <code>status</code> of <code>declined</code> and <code>notPerformedReason.concept</code> of <code>outofstock</code>. Whether the Task is then left open, so a refill retries it, or closed as failed, is the unit's <code>keepOrders</code> setting.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 5</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /Task/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>: <code>status</code> becomes <code>completed</code>, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>. Sent with <code>If-Match</code>, so a Task somebody else has moved on is not overwritten.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 6</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /MedicationRequest/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>. The placer closes its own order. The unit does not: it was asked to fill one Task, and it has no way of knowing whether the order authorized more than that.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></div><div xml:lang=\"nl\" lang=\"nl\"><hr/><p><b>Dutch</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Gegenereerde narrative: ExampleScenario TaskOrderScenario</b></p><a name=\"nl-TaskOrderScenario\"> </a><a name=\"nl-hcTaskOrderScenario\"> </a><p><b>url</b>: <a href=\"ExampleScenario-TaskOrderScenario.html\">Ordering through an order server</a></p><p><b>version</b>: 1.0.0</p><p><b>name</b>: TaskOrderScenario</p><p><b>title</b>: Ordering through an order server</p><p><b>status</b>: actief</p><p><b>experimental</b>: true</p><p><b>date</b>: 2026-11-13 21:21:03+0000</p><p><b>publisher</b>: José Costa Teixeira</p><p><b>contact</b>: José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"https://github.com/costateixeira\">https://github.com/costateixeira</a>, José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"mailto:you-know.it@gmail.com\">you-know.it@gmail.com</a></p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A placer puts an order and a Task on an order server. The unit polls the server, dispenses what is addressed to it, and reports back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>jurisdiction</b>: <span title=\"Codes:{http://unstats.un.org/unsd/methods/m49/m49.htm 001}\">World</span></p><p><b>purpose</b>: </p><div><p>The long way round, and the one that behaves like a real workflow.</p>\n<p>An order on a server is an authorization: it says a chocolate may be dispensed,\nnot that one should be dispensed now. Something else has to ask for it to be\nfulfilled. A Task is that something, and <code>Task.requestedPerformer</code> is the only\nplace in R5 that can name the Device meant to do the work.</p>\n<p>The unit is never connected to from outside here. It polls, which is what lets\na dispenser sit on a conference network with nothing open to it.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: placer</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Placer</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Creates the order and the Task, and closes the order once the Task is done. A Task closes itself; a MedicationRequest does not.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: server</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A plain FHIR server. It holds the order and the Task until a unit collects them, and it has to answer <code>_include=Task:focus</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: spenser</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Spenser Unit</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Acting here as a FHIR client. It takes only the work addressed to it and leaves everything else alone.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationRequest\">All FHIR Types: MedicationRequest</a> (MedicationRequest)</p><p><b>structureProfile</b>: <a href=\"StructureDefinition-SpenserRequest.html\">SpenserRequest</a></p><p><b>title</b>: The order</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>An untagged MedicationRequest, naming the unit meant to fill it in the <code>dispensingDevice</code> extension. On its own it sits there.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest: extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-active</p><p><b>title</b>: active</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created: authorized, and not yet filled.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest: extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the placer closes it. The unit does not touch the order while a Task is coordinating the work.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-Task\">All FHIR Types: Task</a> (Task)</p><p><b>title</b>: The Task</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A <code>fulfill</code> Task whose <code>focus</code> is the order and whose <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. This is what makes the order actionable.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-requested</p><p><b>title</b>: requested</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created. Every other unit polling the same server skips it.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the chocolate came out, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: dispense</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationDispense\">All FHIR Types: MedicationDispense</a> (MedicationDispense)</p><p><b>title</b>: The dispense</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>What the unit writes back, naming itself as <code>performer</code> and the order in <code>authorizingPrescription</code>.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationDispense-DispenseForTaskOrder.html\">MedicationDispense: status = completed</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>process</b></p><p><b>title</b>: Order a chocolate through an order server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Place the work, let the unit find it, and read back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>preConditions</b>: </p><div><p>The unit has been pointed at the order server and its polling is on. The unit has written its own Device on the server, so a Task can name it.</p>\n</div><p><b>postConditions</b>: </p><div><p>A chocolate has been dispensed, the dispense is on the server, the Task is completed, and the order is closed.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 1</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Nothing happens yet, and that is the point.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-active</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 2</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>code</code> is <code>fulfill</code>, <code>focus</code> is the order, <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. Leave <code>requestedPerformer</code> out and any unit polling that server may take it.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>Tag the order instead of creating a Task</td><td><div><p>Put <code>actionable</code> from common-tags in the order's <code>meta.tag</code> and skip the Task. A unit accepts both routes on every check, and <code>orderMode</code> narrows it to one. With no Task coordinating the work the unit completes the MedicationRequest itself, and step 6 does not happen.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 3</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-search-type\">FHIR Restful Interactions: search-type</a> (search-type)</p><p><b>title</b>: GET /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>GET /Task?status=requested&amp;_include=Task:focus&amp;_count=5</code>. The unit polls on a timer, and a check can also be asked for by hand. Each check looks at the first five results only, so a long queue on the server can outrun one check. The unit remembers what it has already dealt with.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Responses</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 4</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationDispense</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>The servo turns and a piece drops out, and then the unit says so. The write is queued and retried, so a server that was briefly unreachable does not cost the record.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>dispense</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>The lane is empty</td><td><div><p>The unit writes a dispense with <code>status</code> of <code>declined</code> and <code>notPerformedReason.concept</code> of <code>outofstock</code>. Whether the Task is then left open, so a refill retries it, or closed as failed, is the unit's <code>keepOrders</code> setting.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 5</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /Task/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>: <code>status</code> becomes <code>completed</code>, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>. Sent with <code>If-Match</code>, so a Task somebody else has moved on is not overwritten.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 6</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /MedicationRequest/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>. The placer closes its own order. The unit does not: it was asked to fill one Task, and it has no way of knowing whether the order authorized more than that.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></div><div xml:lang=\"fr\" lang=\"fr\"><hr/><p><b>French</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Narratif généré : ExampleScenario TaskOrderScenario</b></p><a name=\"fr-TaskOrderScenario\"> </a><a name=\"fr-hcTaskOrderScenario\"> </a><p><b>url</b>: <a href=\"ExampleScenario-TaskOrderScenario.html\">Ordering through an order server</a></p><p><b>version</b>: 1.0.0</p><p><b>name</b>: TaskOrderScenario</p><p><b>title</b>: Ordering through an order server</p><p><b>status</b>: Active</p><p><b>experimental</b>: true</p><p><b>date</b>: 2026-11-13 21:21:03+0000</p><p><b>publisher</b>: José Costa Teixeira</p><p><b>contact</b>: José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"https://github.com/costateixeira\">https://github.com/costateixeira</a>, José Costa Teixeira: <a href=\"mailto:you-know.it@gmail.com\">you-know.it@gmail.com</a></p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A placer puts an order and a Task on an order server. The unit polls the server, dispenses what is addressed to it, and reports back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>jurisdiction</b>: <span title=\"Codes :{http://unstats.un.org/unsd/methods/m49/m49.htm 001}\">World</span></p><p><b>purpose</b>: </p><div><p>The long way round, and the one that behaves like a real workflow.</p>\n<p>An order on a server is an authorization: it says a chocolate may be dispensed,\nnot that one should be dispensed now. Something else has to ask for it to be\nfulfilled. A Task is that something, and <code>Task.requestedPerformer</code> is the only\nplace in R5 that can name the Device meant to do the work.</p>\n<p>The unit is never connected to from outside here. It polls, which is what lets\na dispenser sit on a conference network with nothing open to it.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: placer</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Placer</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Creates the order and the Task, and closes the order once the Task is done. A Task closes itself; a MedicationRequest does not.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: server</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Order Server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A plain FHIR server. It holds the order and the Task until a unit collects them, and it has to answer <code>_include=Task:focus</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>actor</b></p><p><b>key</b>: spenser</p><p><b>type</b>: System</p><p><b>title</b>: Spenser Unit</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Acting here as a FHIR client. It takes only the work addressed to it and leaves everything else alone.</p>\n</div></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationRequest\">All FHIR Types: MedicationRequest</a> (MedicationRequest)</p><p><b>structureProfile</b>: <a href=\"StructureDefinition-SpenserRequest.html\">SpenserRequest</a></p><p><b>title</b>: The order</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>An untagged MedicationRequest, naming the unit meant to fill it in the <code>dispensingDevice</code> extension. On its own it sits there.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest : extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-active</p><p><b>title</b>: active</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created: authorized, and not yet filled.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationRequest-PlainDarkOrderForOneUnit.html\">MedicationRequest : extension = -&gt;Spenser-E3D4; status = active; intent = instance-order</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: order-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the placer closes it. The unit does not touch the order while a Task is coordinating the work.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-Task\">All FHIR Types: Task</a> (Task)</p><p><b>title</b>: The Task</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>A <code>fulfill</code> Task whose <code>focus</code> is the order and whose <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. This is what makes the order actionable.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-requested</p><p><b>title</b>: requested</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>As created. Every other unit polling the same server skips it.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"Task-FulfillForOneUnit.html\">Task Fulfill the focal request</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>version</b></p><p><b>key</b>: task-completed</p><p><b>title</b>: completed</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>After the chocolate came out, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>.</p>\n</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>instance</b></p><p><b>key</b>: dispense</p><p><b>structureType</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-fhir-types.html#fhir-types-MedicationDispense\">All FHIR Types: MedicationDispense</a> (MedicationDispense)</p><p><b>title</b>: The dispense</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>What the unit writes back, naming itself as <code>performer</code> and the order in <code>authorizingPrescription</code>.</p>\n</div><p><b>content</b>: <a href=\"MedicationDispense-DispenseForTaskOrder.html\">MedicationDispense : status = completed</a></p></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>process</b></p><p><b>title</b>: Order a chocolate through an order server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Place the work, let the unit find it, and read back what it did.</p>\n</div><p><b>preConditions</b>: </p><div><p>The unit has been pointed at the order server and its polling is on. The unit has written its own Device on the server, so a Task can name it.</p>\n</div><p><b>postConditions</b>: </p><div><p>A chocolate has been dispensed, the dispense is on the server, the Task is completed, and the order is closed.</p>\n</div><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 1</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>Nothing happens yet, and that is the point.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-active</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 2</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>code</code> is <code>fulfill</code>, <code>focus</code> is the order, <code>requestedPerformer</code> is the unit. Leave <code>requestedPerformer</code> out and any unit polling that server may take it.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>Tag the order instead of creating a Task</td><td><div><p>Put <code>actionable</code> from common-tags in the order's <code>meta.tag</code> and skip the Task. A unit accepts both routes on every check, and <code>orderMode</code> narrows it to one. With no Task coordinating the work the unit completes the MedicationRequest itself, and step 6 does not happen.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 3</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-search-type\">FHIR Restful Interactions: search-type</a> (search-type)</p><p><b>title</b>: GET /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>GET /Task?status=requested&amp;_include=Task:focus&amp;_count=5</code>. The unit polls on a timer, and a check can also be asked for by hand. Each check looks at the first five results only, so a long queue on the server can outrun one check. The unit remembers what it has already dealt with.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Responses</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-requested</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 4</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-create\">FHIR Restful Interactions: create</a> (create)</p><p><b>title</b>: POST /MedicationDispense</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p>The servo turns and a piece drops out, and then the unit says so. The write is queued and retried, so a server that was briefly unreachable does not cost the record.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>dispense</td></tr></table></blockquote><h3>Alternatives</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>The lane is empty</td><td><div><p>The unit writes a dispense with <code>status</code> of <code>declined</code> and <code>notPerformedReason.concept</code> of <code>outofstock</code>. Whether the Task is then left open, so a refill retries it, or closed as failed, is the unit's <code>keepOrders</code> setting.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 5</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /Task</p><p><b>initiator</b>: spenser</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /Task/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>: <code>status</code> becomes <code>completed</code>, with the dispense in <code>Task.output</code>. Sent with <code>If-Match</code>, so a Task somebody else has moved on is not overwritten.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>task</td><td>task-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote><p><b>step</b></p><p><b>number</b>: 6</p><blockquote><p><b>operation</b></p><p><b>type</b>: <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-restful-interaction.html#restful-interaction-update\">FHIR Restful Interactions: update</a> (update)</p><p><b>title</b>: PUT /MedicationRequest</p><p><b>initiator</b>: placer</p><p><b>receiver</b>: server</p><p><b>description</b>: </p><div><p><code>PUT /MedicationRequest/\\&lt;id&gt;</code>. The placer closes its own order. The unit does not: it was asked to fill one Task, and it has no way of knowing whether the order authorized more than that.</p>\n</div><p><b>initiatorActive</b>: true</p><p><b>receiverActive</b>: true</p><h3>Requests</h3><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td style=\"display: none\">-</td><td><b>InstanceReference</b></td><td><b>VersionReference</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"display: none\">*</td><td>order</td><td>order-completed</td></tr></table></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></div></div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral ]
  ] ; # 
  fhir:url [ fhir:v "http://costateixeira.github.io/spenser/ExampleScenario/TaskOrderScenario"^^xsd:anyURI] ; # 
  fhir:version [ fhir:v "1.0.0"] ; # 
  fhir:name [ fhir:v "TaskOrderScenario"] ; # 
  fhir:title [ fhir:v "Ordering through an order server"] ; # 
